i have a problem with productivity  it all begins with a very simple idea  that more of a good thing  is better productivity guru productivity  productivity equals productivity apps  how i stay productive extremely  productive toxic relationship with  productivity  so we try to be faster more efficient  less lazy  but like everything the further you go  down that rabbit hole  the less innocent things become my  channel is  tiny but i'm still contributing to this  online world of youtube  productivity and even though in my head  i'm very very clear  on my issues with it this is not  something i have necessarily discussed  on this channel before  so today here it goes these are all of  my issues  with youtube productivity firstly it  uses universal measures  for when to wake up for how much work to  do in a day for the fact that everyone  can afford a full-time job and a few  side hustles it has little to no regard  for different people's attention spans  for the fact that some people may be  parents  for the fact that some people may not  earn as much money or for the fact that  people may have different stress levels  or even learning disabilities very often  what is not seen is that these very  productive and successful people online  actually have huge teams in the  background which are helping them with  this workload  they might even have people cooking for  them or taking care of their kids or  just money to afford crazy holidays to  decompress from this crazy productive  time  so things are not as simple as they seem  online and these universal measures of  you can do it too are probably not  true next i feel like productivity makes  you respect yourself conditionally  so only if you do as much work as you  plan to do in that certain day or in  that certain hour or in that certain  week or month  only then can you feel good about  yourself you're probably going to end up  on one or more nights going to bed  feeling angry at yourself  feeling displeased with yourself and not  feeling at peace unless you complete  these quotas that you've set up in your  mind and this is probably not a good  long-term relationship to have next  effect productivity kind of puts you in  a bit of a parental role with yourself  where you're talking down to yourself  you're not listening to your excuses and  you're trying to  you know know what is best and make  yourself do things all the time while  ignoring your needs to do something else  or to do nothing at all and i feel like  this is not a good  long-term relationship to have sometimes  there are real reasons that you don't  want to do something and perhaps  listening  to yourself or your body when you just  don't feel like working is a good thing  maybe you need a break maybe you need to  socialize maybe you need to help other  people or feel valuable in a community  or society which is something that  productivity doesn't focus too much on  and i feel like it is a great loss in  the long term to be this kind of abusive  parent  to yourself next i feel as though it  might make one thing that if they're  following these formulas which are so  honestly given to you online that you  should achieve what other people have  achieved although most decent people who  are talking about productivity are not  guaranteeing this i feel as though over  the long term it may be something that  you feel  as in i'm trying to do the exact same  things why am i not getting the same  results  and it has little regard to things such  as luck or how much money these people  have before they started doing these  things or what emotional state they have  been  or what is their mental health like or  how they look for example i feel as  though these things don't play very  often into the productivity equation  online liver can leave me as a consumer  sometimes feeling as though i  must be doing something wrong i am  eternally dissatisfied with my results  in fact just being productive and  adapting these tips will get you nowhere  if you're not headed in the right  direction i love the phrase of if your  ladder is up against the wrong wall  you'll just get to the wrong place  faster  for a lot of people who have gotten  lucky and successful going in the right  direction is just as important as the  productivity tips that they have used to  get there  so if you're just using these tips but  you're going in the whole opposite  direction  you're probably not going to get to the  same results and this is not something  that is generally discussed next i feel  as though it puts you at competition  with yourself at best and with the world  at  worst you're always competing to be  better than you were last month or last  year and also quite often to be better  than everyone else around you  and although there's nothing wrong with  a bit of healthy competition i feel like  productivity relies on it  quite a lot because you need to see  improvement and do things better  and if you want to see that you've used  the productivity tips you surely now  must be faster than you were yesterday  so i feel as though this constant strive  for more and more and more is probably  not the healthiest way to live your life  next i feel like  productivity generally makes you selfish  and this is because it is just focused  internally on the person  so what did i do today how did this  impact myself how do i feel about what i  did  it doesn't really have to do a lot with  other people around me  and very often being very productive  just makes the people who care the most  about you and around you  feel worse because they're not seeing as  much of you and you're just so  self-involved in whatever you are doing  and of course there's nothing wrong with  doing what you want to do and being on  your own  i just feel like this level of  selfishness is probably something that  needs to be counter balanced with other  things which are not necessarily  discussed as much in the productivity  realm next i feel quite strongly about  this productivity is mostly focused on  the results  so how do you get more results for less  time how to get the same results for  less time  how do you get more and more and more of  everything rather than what are the  actual things that you are  achieving and how much are you enjoying  the process i feel as though enjoying  the process  is very cheesy but it's also super super  important in the extreme end in the  realm of productivity  pain can be a good thing or even a badge  of honor as in the less you sleep the  less you've talked to your family the  less you  spend doing nothing so basically the  less you respect yourself the better off  you are  i just find this to be extremely  extremely toxic so yes at the end of the  day of course i will continue making  productivity content because i  absolutely love it  i just want to say that i also feel very  strongly against it in more than one way  and in my personal life i do try to  counter balance it as much as possible  and this is something that perhaps i  will try to incorporate in my videos a  bit more  yes if you want to have a browse of my  current productivity content please feel  free to look around  otherwise thank you so much for watching  i hope you have a wonderful rest of your  day be kind yourself and others and  don't believe everything you think  thanks  [Music]  bye
 

